    "Aeron leader-side member observations show reported log positions caught up. This summary does not inspect physical hosts or prove independent hardware failure domains.",
    "Canonical snapshot/retry verification uses the deterministic core implementation. It is not an independent matching implementation or a formal distributed-systems proof.",
    "Snapshot logs expose the same core hash and outbox exported/pending counters; this summary does not independently compare every outbox payload.",
    "The 1182 command high-water mark includes setup and warmup as well as measured business commands. It is not a capacity measurement.",
    "No new 900-command post-recovery workload, PostgreSQL projection, browser session, or subsequent business-run evidence is included in this recovery-only summary.",
    "Recovery verifier JSON timestamps identify invocation start, not fault start or completion. Their per-probe elapsed values must not be reported as pure failover or cold-restart RTO."
